  "id": "learning-set",
  "term": "learning set",
  "definition": "A learning set is the whole collection of material learned in a task, such as all the category–exemplar pairs studied before later testing or restudy. In this source, initial retrieval of the full learning set reduced later forgetting of related items after selective retrieval.",
